 "sentences": [
  "Now, when it comes to troubleshooting, it's crucial to have a systematic approach.",
  "Structured problem-solving is key in our line of work.",
  "When naming attributes in your Python code, always start the name with 'j_'.",
  "This is a convention we use here at ZENITH to maintain consistency and improve code readability.",
  "Consistency is important, especially when working with a large code base and collaborating with others.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns about this or anything else.",
  "Absolutely, having the right tools is essential for your productivity and overall experience.",
  "It's important that you have everything you need to succeed in your role.",
  "I'll put in the requests right away and keep you posted on the progress.",
  "It's important to develop good habits right from the start.",
  "Remember, if you ever get stuck or need a second opinion, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "Now, while you work on the interface, I also want you to keep an eye on the overall structure of the program.",
  "We need to ensure it's modular and easy to maintain.",
  "It's important that you feel supported and that your questions are answered.",
  "From now on, I want you to start attribute names with the prefix 't_'.",
  "This will help us maintain consistency and quickly identify attributes within our code base.",
  "Additionally, for method names, include the string 'chx' somewhere in the name.",
  "This will be a unique identifier for our methods and will make them easily recognizable."
 ],
